  "intro": [
    "Every EventBridge operation the emulator advertises, and what Emuplane does with",
    "it. Requests are JSON with an `X-Amz-Target` naming the action, signed with the",
    "`events` credential scope; there is no console action.",
    "Buses, rules, targets, archives, connections, API destinations and global",
    "endpoints are records. A rule's target is validated but not delivered to, so the",
    "tests need no consumer. An archive stores the events a matching publish sends it,",
    "and a replay of an archive with no matching events completes synchronously — the",
    "reachable `CancelReplay` answer is therefore the \"already completed\" refusal.",
    "A global endpoint is accepted only with an existing Route53 health check (created",
    "under the `route53` scope) and two same-named buses in the primary and secondary",
    "regions; replication is disabled in the test so no IAM role is needed. Stable",
    "names carry the read and update rows; delete actions make their own resource."
  ],
